# Crystal Obelisk: the small cross-shaped pyramid of Ender IO 1.12's obelisks (ObeliskBakery).
# Two crossing arms, 0.475 blocks tall: 0.506 wide, 0.9 long at the bottom, tapering to 0.5 long at the top.
# Block units (0..1). Faces are counter-clockwise seen from outside; vt v = 0 at the bottom (flip_v in the JSON).
mtllib crystal_obelisk.mtl

# Arm along Z (x 0.246875 .. 0.753125): bottom 1-4, top 5-8
v 0.246875 0 0.05
v 0.753125 0 0.05
v 0.753125 0 0.95
v 0.246875 0 0.95
v 0.246875 0.475 0.25
v 0.753125 0.475 0.25
v 0.753125 0.475 0.75
v 0.246875 0.475 0.75
# Arm along X (z 0.246875 .. 0.753125): bottom 9-12, top 13-16
v 0.05 0 0.246875
v 0.95 0 0.246875
v 0.95 0 0.753125
v 0.05 0 0.753125
v 0.25 0.475 0.246875
v 0.75 0.475 0.246875
v 0.75 0.475 0.753125
v 0.25 0.475 0.753125
# Underside 17-20
v 0.05 0 0.05
v 0.95 0 0.05
v 0.95 0 0.95
v 0.05 0 0.95

# UVs: 1 top-left, 2 bottom-left, 3 bottom-right, 4 top-right
vt 0 1
vt 0 0
vt 1 0
vt 1 1

usemtl top
# Top (+Y): north-west, south-west, south-east, north-east
f 5/1 8/2 7/3 6/4

usemtl side
# Arm Z: north slope, south slope, west and east flanks
f 6/1 2/2 1/3 5/4
f 8/1 4/2 3/3 7/4
f 5/1 1/2 4/3 8/4
f 7/1 3/2 2/3 6/4
# Arm X: west slope, east slope, north and south flanks
f 13/1 9/2 12/3 16/4
f 15/1 11/2 10/3 14/4
f 14/1 10/2 9/3 13/4
f 16/1 12/2 11/3 15/4

usemtl bottom
f 17/1 18/2 19/3 20/4
